What is bitcoin? Here’s the lowdown on the digital currency
Bitcoin is a digital currency that operates outside of traditional banking systems, which means it is not tied to any central bank or government. In other words, there is no central authority that controls the Bitcoin network, and there is no single central Bitcoin exchange.
Bitcoin was invented in 2009 by an unknown person or group of people using the pseudonym Satoshi Nakamoto. Bitcoin is a peer-to-peer payment system that is not managed by any central authority. Instead, Bitcoin is managed by a network of computers that are connected to the Internet.
